      "historical_evidence_messages": [
        {
          "message_id": 13,
          "conversation_turn_index": 13,
          "speaker": "client",
          "text": "Dom,\n\nCould you provide a total quote for 96-102 pages?\n\nThanks!\nNate",
          "created_ts": null,
          "original_index": 12
        },
        {
          "message_id": 15,
          "conversation_turn_index": 15,
          "speaker": "client",
          "text": "The original book contains 8 parts, and I’m considering the first four parts for the initial graphic novel. I can send you the relevant files tomorrow morning. Production costs are still being finalized, and the crowdfunding campaign is scheduled to launch on Thursday, so I’d appreciate receiving your quote two days beforehand. Thanks!",
          "created_ts": null,
          "original_index": 14
        },
        {
          "message_id": 17,
          "conversation_turn_index": 17,
          "speaker": "freelancer",
          "text": "Using what I had already written, I worked through the numbers.\n\nFirst, could you clarify whether the request is for 102 pages of screenplay or 102 pages of comic? My completed work produced an approximate screenplay-to-comic conversion of roughly 3:1.\n\nIf part 4 is approximately the same length as episode 1, then parts 1 through 4 should amount to around 54-60 comic pages. I could complete that scope for $625 with a turnaround of 5 weeks. If I can reuse 18 pages from the sample script with only light revision and page reflowing, I could reduce that price to $475.\n\nThe larger option of 96-102 comic pages is also possible, but it would require covering more of the story, presumably through episode 5 or 6. For that scope, I propose $1125 with a 7-week turnaround. With 18 pages of the sample script reused, the price would instead be $950.\n\nPlease let me know which option is closer to what you have in mind and whether these terms work for you.\n\nThanks,\nDom",
          "created_ts": null,
          "original_index": 16
        }
      ]
